Freedom Of Information Response to Safe Schools Materials Request. DET FOI 2018-329
Thank you for your recent response.
7 All the recommended teacher resources under the HPE curriculum, sexual health, bullying and sexuality education. This includes all suggested and inferred third party organisations including but not limited to, Minus18, Project Rockit, “Beyond That’s So Gay” – Daniel Witthaus, all AnsellSex-Ed.
The relevant key links relating to this part of your request are as follows: (PLEASE NOTE THAT THE FIRST LINK NO LONGER WORKS.)
Please be advised that none of these resources are mandated. They are optional for schools to use, and teachers exercise their professional judgement in selecting and using resources which are appropriate to their school context and their student cohort.
We also wish to advise you of the first six points of your request, being:
2 All materials relating to the ‘Safe Schools’ program that have been implemented by the Department of Education and Training for every year level within Secondary Schools, whether expressly as part of the ‘Safe Schools’ program or within other areas of the curriculum.
4 Any student workbooks that have been created, published, distributed or utilised in relation to the ‘Safe Schools’ program across both Primary and Secondary Schools.
6 Any evidence, both qualitative and quantitative in nature, which is in the possession of the Department of Education and Training, which demonstrates any correlation (whether positive or negative) between the ‘Safe Schools’ program and student learning outcomes. This includes evidence obtained in relation to both Primary Schools and Secondary Schools.
