HOW WE IMPACT CHILDREN
As a microfinance organization and a subsidiary of World Vision, WB Finance Cambodia has a vision for every child, life in all its fullness. We provide small loans and other financial services to empower women, unlock the potential of communities to flourish and ultimately enable children to grow up healthy.
Loan to Promote Child Rights: In collaboration with International labor Organization, as of December 2015, an estimated 8,448 children have so far been impacted by loans of US $3,852,550 given to the familes of the targeted groups in Phnom Penh, its ourskirts, Kampong Cham and Siem Reap who’ve got better access to education instead of needing to work to support their families.
In cooperation with WVC, as of December 2015,5,093 WB Finance clients have received basic health training session mainly covered on dengue fever, diarrhea, food demonstration, hand washing, nutrition, and general hygiene, which resulted in a better health care for children.
In 2015, there were 827 students who received loans to study in higher education in education in a bachelor and master degree program or to attend any vocational training skill program for their future profession. The total portfolio is US $530,477.
By the end of December 2015, WB Finance provides loans to 33,396 households to buy water filter so that families members and children can have access to clean drinking water.
