When you’re using wood chips to smoke your favorite meaty cuts, you know that the secret lies in smoking at the perfect temperature.
Therefore, you’ve got to get your wood chips to the right temperature until they smolder.
Wood chips smoke at a temperature between 570-750 degrees Fahrenheit, or 300-400 degrees Celsius. All wood chips smoke when they reach these temperatures, but some woods burn and smolder at a faster rate than others.
As you know, smoke is extremely important for your foods because it gives meat that aroma and flavor you can only achieve by smoking.
4 Should You Soak Wood Chips?
Each wood has a different flavor; thus, you’ll get a much stronger aroma from hickory than from a light fruitwood like apple, for example.
When I talk about the ideal temp for wood chips to smoke, I refer to the actual wood chips’ temperature, not the heat inside the smoker or grill.
Be sure to check the chips themselves and not the air inside the smoker if you’re noticing issues with the smoke.
7 types of smokers explained.
Since you want to get to that temperature where the chips start to smoke, you need to control the heat.
The theory behind this is that as wood burns, it produces heat mostly and very little smoke.
It takes about 20 minutes for wood chips to start to smoke in your smoker or the smoker accessory.
So, is it really necessary to soak them?
In fact, if you soak the chips for an hour or so, they will actually release more steam, not more flavorful smoke.
The wood chips must eliminate all that moisture first before they begin to smolder and smoke.
Therefore, you have to wait a bit longer to get your smoke.
Many smokers complain about some types of wood chips not creating enough smoke for a whole smoking session.
Cold outside?
