4 Gas vs Electric Smoker: Which is Better
There are quite a few distinguishing factors that make electric smokers unique from other types of smokers on the market.
The control panel is what you use to determine temperature settings and you can use it to customize the smoking process by choosing a particular type of meat.
From there, the smoker can easily operate for five hours on the same wood chips and without constant supervision. Plus, all you need is four wood chip cups that will last for that entire time period.
The digital control panel allows you to “set it and forget it” so you can spend more of your time socializing instead of constantly checking on the meat.
They’re safer to use thanks to the integrated insulation, which is a missing feature in most gas smokers.
It’s pricier than its gas counterparts.
The quality of the food smoked by an electric smoker pales in comparison to that of a gas smoker.
You can’t use it without electricity access.
It has a limited temperature range that only goes up to 300 degrees Fahrenheit. A natural gas smoker, on the other hand, can go up to 400 degrees Fahrenheit, allowing you to smoke meat at high temperatures.
The only difference is that gas smokers are a bit more demanding of your attention and they require quite a bit of oversight.
The type of wood chips you put into the smoker will play a huge role in the smoker’s temperature and the flavor of your meat.
It’s easy to use and doesn’t require any technical experience to set up or operate.
It has a wide temperature range which gives you more freedom when smoking different types of meat.
It’s time-consuming. You need to be present at all times to regulate the temperature because none of its functions are automatic.
A fair amount of know-how is required if you want to make the most of your gas smoker.
It’s not insulated and can be hazardous to handle if you’re not familiar with it.
Now that you more or less understand what each option has to offer, we’re going to compare the two based on a few key features.
Lastly, we’ll reveal what our preferred option is between the two and why we recommend it specifically.
